WEBVTT

00:02.000 --> 00:03.270
<i>Give them back.</i>

00:15.850 --> 00:17.020
<i>Give them back.</i>

00:18.790 --> 00:20.150
<i>Give them back!</i>

00:20.150 --> 00:21.630
<i>Give us back our children!</i>

00:22.990 --> 00:28.600
<i>Bring our children back to our pack!</i>

00:29.240 --> 00:30.520
<i>Give them back!</i>

01:10.860 --> 01:13.330
Whoa, what's gotten into you?

01:13.570 --> 01:14.580
Nothing...

01:15.520 --> 01:18.670
Someone just cried somewhere.

01:19.720 --> 01:21.010
Say what?

01:21.760 --> 01:25.700
I wonder what they're grieving over.

03:03.920 --> 03:05.770
Hold it!

03:04.250 --> 03:05.590
Come on!

03:05.770 --> 03:07.420
Now what?

03:07.420 --> 03:08.670
Whoa, whoa, what's that?!

03:09.580 --> 03:11.030
There.

03:13.720 --> 03:15.380
Why are we tilling fields

03:15.380 --> 03:19.220
right after we've gotten the crap
 beaten out of us by monsters?

03:19.220 --> 03:23.760
With the College closed, we're going 
to have to grow our own food.

03:32.110 --> 03:33.000
Hey.

03:33.490 --> 03:36.860
We were just talking about how 
awesome you were back there, Rian.

03:36.860 --> 03:37.980
Ah.

03:38.600 --> 03:41.730
My family needs to be quick to react.

03:42.220 --> 03:46.210
You weren't like that in the past, though.

03:46.570 --> 03:48.750
You even sucked at climbing trees.

03:51.760 --> 03:53.340
I just hated losing.

03:55.740 --> 03:56.780
Huh...

03:56.780 --> 03:58.030
Losing to who?

03:58.030 --> 03:59.700
I don't want to tell you.

04:00.460 --> 04:01.510
Wow.

04:02.540 --> 04:05.020
I-In the past, huh?

04:05.890 --> 04:09.570
Have you two been friends
 since you were little?

04:09.570 --> 04:12.020
Our families have business together.

04:12.020 --> 04:13.390
You there!

04:13.390 --> 04:15.670
I want to see your hands working!

04:15.670 --> 04:17.040
Okay.

04:25.880 --> 04:27.310
Lady Philomela.

04:27.310 --> 04:30.010
Alcyone-san, was it?

04:30.010 --> 04:33.010
Philomela doesn't seem to be feeling well.

04:35.150 --> 04:36.310
I'm putting you down.

04:40.230 --> 04:40.920
Who's she?

04:41.230 --> 04:45.250
Something like Philomela's familiar, I guess.

04:45.600 --> 04:48.170
What's up with that vague answer?

04:50.540 --> 04:51.420
Are you all right?

04:52.280 --> 04:53.820
I'll get some water.

04:53.820 --> 04:55.940
Thanks. Please do.

05:02.750 --> 05:05.150
<i>Her room's so empty.</i>

05:06.400 --> 05:08.010
What was the class?

05:08.880 --> 05:11.680
We each had to destroy a familiar.

05:11.680 --> 05:16.460
This one is very adverse 
to destroying things.

05:16.870 --> 05:19.390
She always falls ill.

05:19.810 --> 05:20.870
Always?

05:21.990 --> 05:24.950
She collapsed the first time we met, too.

05:24.950 --> 05:26.090
Did she?

05:28.470 --> 05:29.690
Um...

05:29.690 --> 05:31.010
Alcyone-san...

05:31.010 --> 05:31.980
Yes?

05:32.440 --> 05:35.270
Is Philomela...

05:40.130 --> 05:45.480
Why do you worry about me so much?

05:47.620 --> 05:51.420
I'm always spying on you and Zoe.

05:52.160 --> 05:54.820
I don't try to talk in front of others.

05:55.240 --> 06:00.130
You ought to be suspicious of me.

06:03.600 --> 06:05.120
You're right.

06:05.900 --> 06:11.370
The first time I met you, 
you weren't feeling well,

06:11.370 --> 06:14.160
and yet you responded to me just to be nice.

06:14.570 --> 06:16.460
You even thanked me.

06:17.070 --> 06:24.190
And, well... To me, you look 
like you're in a lot of pain.

06:26.180 --> 06:28.710
I was like that until just recently, too.

06:29.830 --> 06:34.640
So I thought I might be 
able to hear you out.

06:35.680 --> 06:40.970
Oh, but if there's anything you 
don't want to tell me, that's okay.

06:40.970 --> 06:43.330
If there's something you 
want to say to me, you can.

06:43.900 --> 06:46.230
You're free to do as you like.

06:47.170 --> 06:49.500
Being free is hard,

06:50.400 --> 06:55.080
but even if you make a mistake or 
you fail, you can always try again.

06:55.950 --> 06:57.170
It'll be all right.

07:00.590 --> 07:03.940
I don't understand you.

07:04.330 --> 07:06.000
Freedom?

07:06.560 --> 07:08.500
I can fail?

07:09.190 --> 07:12.040
No one's ever told me that.

07:14.270 --> 07:15.840
I brought water.

07:16.340 --> 07:17.990
Thanks, Lucy.

07:20.120 --> 07:24.470
I don't get what this 
do-gooder's thinking, either.

07:24.820 --> 07:27.730
I'm sure it's just an inflated ego.

07:28.060 --> 07:29.370
What's wrong?

07:29.370 --> 07:30.860
Drink up.

07:30.860 --> 07:32.450
You'll feel a bit better.

07:35.680 --> 07:36.800
Fine.

07:37.480 --> 07:38.950
Let's go, Chise.

07:39.410 --> 07:41.520
Yeah, you're right.

07:41.520 --> 07:43.740
I don't want to overstay my welcome.

07:43.740 --> 07:45.610
Don't push yourself too hard. Get some rest.

07:47.350 --> 07:48.860
Thank you.

07:54.930 --> 07:56.930
I wasted that water.

07:58.250 --> 08:05.160
"You mustn't drink, eat, or use 
anything someone else gives you.

08:05.820 --> 08:08.320
There's no telling what's in it."

08:08.970 --> 08:11.600
That's what some families preach.

08:12.160 --> 08:14.080
Seems her family's that way, too.

08:14.760 --> 08:16.550
Which means...

08:17.100 --> 08:19.670
Could you give me some feedback someday?

08:20.640 --> 08:23.020
Th-Thanks.

08:24.090 --> 08:25.360
What?

08:25.360 --> 08:28.650
I really am egotistic.

08:29.130 --> 08:32.240
Also, Philomela is actually kind.

08:33.580 --> 08:35.990
Everyone's got an ego.

08:36.300 --> 08:41.120
I couldn't trust anyone who always grants 
other people's wishes at their own expense.

08:41.790 --> 08:44.680
There's no telling what 
they might do someday.

08:47.060 --> 08:49.170
You're kind, too.

08:50.090 --> 08:53.920
I don't know what <i>you</i> might do, 
either. I don't trust you.

08:53.920 --> 08:55.730
Huh? Where did that come from?

09:00.440 --> 09:03.090
<i>There's so much I wanted to ask...</i>

09:03.090 --> 09:07.630
<i>But with her in that state, 
I couldn't bring myself to do it.</i>

09:11.670 --> 09:13.620
<i>That kid there that day...</i>

09:15.030 --> 09:20.550
<i>They couldn't have killed a person if they 
had such a hard time killing a familiar.</i>

09:23.050 --> 09:25.030
<i>I need more leads.</i>

09:46.010 --> 09:47.270
Why?

09:49.210 --> 09:50.600
Why can't I...

09:51.870 --> 09:58.520
Why can't I just have some 
water or tea someone's given me?

10:02.090 --> 10:03.820
In the past...

10:05.110 --> 10:06.630
Alcyone.

10:06.630 --> 10:10.610
You accepted everything you were told, 
no matter how upsetting.

10:10.610 --> 10:12.140
You would just submit.

10:12.900 --> 10:14.850
But now, you do not.

10:15.540 --> 10:16.830
Why is that?

10:19.280 --> 10:20.890
I don't know.

10:20.890 --> 10:22.380
Because she...

10:29.830 --> 10:31.100
I don't know.

10:31.640 --> 10:33.070
But...

10:33.070 --> 10:36.700
But I can't do this anymore.

10:39.150 --> 10:42.360
Detected registration of 
new vocabulary cluster.

10:42.890 --> 10:45.010
Playing message.

10:45.470 --> 10:46.420
Alcyone?

10:47.760 --> 10:55.440
Philomela, I will no longer tolerate you 
wasting the chances that I give you.

10:56.430 --> 10:59.040
<i>Grandmother's voice...</i>

10:59.500 --> 11:04.540
<i>There's no way she could communicate or send 
a bird so easily with the College closed off.</i>

11:04.540 --> 11:05.840
<i>A message?</i>

11:05.840 --> 11:09.020
<i>Registered to Alcyone ahead of time?</i>

11:09.020 --> 11:12.230
I have no home to provide 
a failure like you.

11:10.930 --> 11:13.380
<i>So... So that I...</i>

11:13.380 --> 11:17.250
If what you gain is something 
as silly as friendship,

11:17.250 --> 11:21.180
I will have to think of 
a way to deal with you.

11:18.400 --> 11:19.920
<i>I won't run away.</i>

11:21.960 --> 11:24.780
Otherwise, do what you are told.

11:24.780 --> 11:27.120
Carry out your role.

11:27.760 --> 11:31.520
If you wish to see your father and mother,

11:31.520 --> 11:35.630
you shouldn't even have the time to whine.

11:36.050 --> 11:37.530
Playback finished.

11:37.530 --> 11:39.540
Message will be deleted.

11:40.700 --> 11:41.750
Lady Philomela?

11:42.280 --> 11:43.960
Is something the matter?

11:52.880 --> 11:54.300
Shall I assist you?

11:56.930 --> 12:01.020
You must have been aware of how 
troublesome the College's paperwork is.

12:01.020 --> 12:03.960
It's been so long, I'd completely forgotten.

12:03.960 --> 12:07.580
They're just signatures. I'll manage.

12:08.280 --> 12:10.120
Have there since been any more demands

12:10.120 --> 12:12.410
from the Sergeant family 
that she leaves the school?

12:12.850 --> 12:14.330
None so far.

12:14.810 --> 12:18.570
We're keeping an eye on that 
familiar, but from what we can see,

12:18.570 --> 12:20.700
she isn't very capable.

12:21.340 --> 12:26.650
I don't think she's made to accept complex 
commands, let alone carry them out.

12:27.050 --> 12:29.590
I doubt she could do more than babysit.

12:30.240 --> 12:32.380
I suppose we'll have to wait and see.

12:32.810 --> 12:35.400
Has there been anything 
noteworthy since the closure?

12:35.870 --> 12:36.890
Not really.

12:36.890 --> 12:39.320
No one's been attacked since then, either.

12:39.990 --> 12:44.690
I suspect the magic book has 
already been taken outside.

12:45.170 --> 12:49.610
I can't imagine anyone would be 
walking around with that thing.

12:50.720 --> 12:54.580
If we're lucky, the witches will catch them.

13:03.440 --> 13:04.440
Morning.

13:04.440 --> 13:05.100
You're late.

13:05.100 --> 13:06.540
Sorry.

13:06.540 --> 13:11.150
Well, shall we look for 
that missing magic book?

13:45.390 --> 13:46.580
Gross!

13:46.580 --> 13:47.960
That's it?

13:47.960 --> 13:51.400
You really are hundreds of 
years older than me, huh?

13:51.400 --> 13:53.210
You youngins sure know
how to run your mouths!

13:53.210 --> 13:56.800
And you've brought me some bizarre work.

13:56.800 --> 13:59.640
I would have bitten you if 
you weren't one of my own!

14:16.080 --> 14:20.340
The scent is faint, but it's that way.

14:20.950 --> 14:22.080
Let's go.

14:36.380 --> 14:41.350
How did you manage to read 
that magic book, anyway?

14:41.930 --> 14:44.230
My brain's still shaking.

14:44.230 --> 14:48.360
It must have been ten... 
maybe five years ago.

14:48.970 --> 14:57.780
After Phyllis was forced to be shut in,
 I was desperately looking for a solution.

14:58.630 --> 15:04.050
That's when I found a home that was 
selling some magic books and tools.

15:04.790 --> 15:06.600
How unusual.

15:06.600 --> 15:10.290
Isn't that like a sorcerer 
selling their soul?

15:10.760 --> 15:13.490
They must have been really 
struggling financially.

15:13.490 --> 15:15.300
And you bought it?

15:16.180 --> 15:18.030
It would have been a huge waste if I had

15:18.030 --> 15:20.640
and it didn't have
 the information I wanted.

15:20.640 --> 15:23.830
So I begged them to let me skim through it.

15:23.830 --> 15:26.600
Though they ended up 
charging me quite a bit.

15:27.170 --> 15:33.360
But in the end, I didn't want to take 
the heat, so I passed on buying it.

15:33.840 --> 15:35.810
I see.

15:35.810 --> 15:36.920
Hmm...

15:38.270 --> 15:41.150
The scent's definitely getting thinner.

15:41.770 --> 15:45.460
It doesn't seem like 
they're lying in wait...

15:46.090 --> 15:49.460
So much as they're walking 
around to throw us off.

15:50.250 --> 15:52.670
I suppose it's time we pay a visit.

16:17.120 --> 16:18.860
Well, well.

16:19.520 --> 16:22.630
How can I help a witch?

16:22.630 --> 16:25.350
You've even brought a werewolf with you.

16:25.350 --> 16:27.950
Hey, I'm a witch, too.

16:28.210 --> 16:31.880
Have you seen someone walking 
around with a suspicious book?

16:31.880 --> 16:33.290
A suspicious book?

16:33.680 --> 16:35.080
Never mind that.

16:35.080 --> 16:36.000
Look!

16:36.810 --> 16:40.100
Trick boxes to keep imps away.

16:40.100 --> 16:42.070
I'll make it cheap.

16:42.070 --> 16:44.190
Two for one coin.

16:44.650 --> 16:45.570
Well?

16:51.750 --> 16:53.320
I'll take five.

16:55.140 --> 16:58.650
I'd like a little more sugar.

16:58.930 --> 17:01.550
Very well, very well!

17:01.550 --> 17:05.750
I admire a witch who isn't stingy.

17:06.360 --> 17:10.840
I was ready to eat you 
if you'd held back.

17:11.470 --> 17:13.160
Pardon me.

17:19.370 --> 17:21.390
What an awful book.

17:22.300 --> 17:28.500
Any dunce would notice you 
walking around with that.

17:30.160 --> 17:34.900
So much of what humans make is imperfect.

17:35.480 --> 17:39.440
Should I find what you're
 looking for, I'll let you know.

17:39.880 --> 17:45.630
Be sure to bring any good coins you find.

17:53.140 --> 17:57.210
Well, tell me where the naughty child is.

18:14.680 --> 18:15.650
Is it just me, or...

18:15.910 --> 18:17.190
There's a lot.

18:17.190 --> 18:18.240
That's what I thought.

18:18.870 --> 18:25.070
Exams are still a thing, even 
with the College being closed.

18:25.070 --> 18:28.580
Hey, what does this mean?

18:28.580 --> 18:32.310
I can't figure it out, no matter 
how many times I read it.

18:32.310 --> 18:33.550
Which one?

18:36.860 --> 18:39.160
Oh, this one...

18:39.160 --> 18:44.180
Sorry, I skipped this part, 
too. I couldn't understand it.

18:44.180 --> 18:47.690
Wasn't the interpretation 
written in another handout?

18:47.690 --> 18:49.370
Huh?! Where was that?

18:49.730 --> 18:53.430
That part's not sorcery or anything. 
That's just language.

18:53.430 --> 18:54.790
Use a dictionary.

18:54.790 --> 18:58.430
You could be proud of me 
just for speaking English.

18:58.730 --> 19:03.290
College English sure is hard.

19:04.070 --> 19:07.510
Forget sorcery, this is a bigger problem.

19:08.220 --> 19:10.400
You're a mage, aren't you?

19:10.400 --> 19:12.340
Does this even matter to you?

19:12.340 --> 19:18.720
I'm exempt from having to do magic stuff, 
but I still have to earn credits.

19:18.720 --> 19:21.210
So, what's there "a lot" of?

19:21.470 --> 19:22.600
The golems.

19:23.080 --> 19:25.550
They were always wandering 
the yard and garden floors,

19:26.150 --> 19:29.050
but they're on the other normal floors, too.

19:29.050 --> 19:30.590
Almost like guards.

19:31.830 --> 19:34.180
We were attacked from the outside.

19:34.180 --> 19:36.180
Of course there are some guards around.

19:36.180 --> 19:37.910
That's true.

19:38.390 --> 19:39.980
I'm going to look for references.

19:40.480 --> 19:41.330
Okay.

19:45.160 --> 19:49.660
<i>Lucy doesn't intend to tell anyone 
she was the one who was attacked.</i>

20:02.840 --> 20:04.420
<i>She left.</i>

20:05.490 --> 20:06.090
<i>Huh?</i>

20:11.130 --> 20:13.920
<i>Alcyone-san is kind of...</i>

20:15.060 --> 20:18.780
<i>She's like Elias if he were a child.</i>

20:22.320 --> 20:26.670
Chise, Zoe, I found a useful textbook.

20:26.670 --> 20:27.700
Come read it.

20:27.700 --> 20:29.360
Really?

20:29.360 --> 20:30.630
You found one for us?

20:30.840 --> 20:32.280
Thanks!

20:32.280 --> 20:33.510
I just came across it.

20:35.720 --> 20:38.760
Rian, do you have a crush on Philomela?

20:38.760 --> 20:39.540
Huh?!

20:41.140 --> 20:43.340
You're pretty prickly towards her.

20:43.340 --> 20:48.170
I figured it might be that classic 
annoying type of affection.

20:49.130 --> 20:51.340
I already know who <i>the one</i> is for me.

20:52.070 --> 20:54.150
And she's not it.

20:54.660 --> 20:58.650
I just find it frustrating when people 
don't know their own self-worth.

20:59.460 --> 21:00.930
What about you?

21:00.930 --> 21:01.730
Me?

21:02.300 --> 21:04.730
You seem to protect her from me a lot.

21:05.330 --> 21:06.820
What's the idea?

21:09.890 --> 21:11.420
What do <i>you</i> think?

21:12.280 --> 21:14.590
Ow! Ow! Ow!

21:14.590 --> 21:15.930
Stop it, idiot!

21:15.930 --> 21:17.420
Stop twisting!

21:16.050 --> 21:19.040
I hate when people don't 
give me a straight answer.

21:18.300 --> 21:19.980
Ow, ow, ow!

21:19.980 --> 21:21.010
I hate it.

21:20.340 --> 21:21.630
What are they doing?

21:26.020 --> 21:27.120
Principal.

21:29.810 --> 21:31.080
Well.

21:31.080 --> 21:34.020
The witches have returned from their duties.

21:34.600 --> 21:37.060
Thank you, mister gatekeeper.

21:57.440 --> 22:01.890
So the dreaded book is still in the College.

22:20.410 --> 22:23.970
Maybe I'm thirsty or something.
